    "The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the approved plans and documents as set out in the attached schedule which forms part of this notice.\r\rLocation Plan - BR.35.LP\rProposed Floor  and Elevations Plan - BR.35.PR.101\rProposed Section AA\rFlood Risk Assessment\rDesign and Access Statement\rDaylight and Sunlight Assessment\r\rReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interests of proper planning\r",
    "The site shall not be occupied until site plans showing that the proposed cycle store falls within the development boundary have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. If this cannot be achieved, an off-site cycle parking contribution should be agreed with Transport Officers.\r\rReason: To ensure the cycle parking at the site does not encroach and impede the public highway.\r",
    "The site shall not be occupied until further details regarding the refuse arrangements at the site have been submitted to and approved in writing by the Local Planning Authority. This must include the location of the bin store alongside the number and types of bins provided. The applicant must also demonstrate how the location and provision meets Enfield household waste and recycling planning guidance and Manual for Streets guidance. \r\rReason: To ensure the site conforms to Enfield household waste and recycling planning guidance and Enfield DMD Policy 47.\r"
